{
  "name": "Driver COD Briefing",
  "description": "Every morning at 9am Edmonton: calls the RxDeliver driverCodBriefing function (via REST, since workflow function invokes run in the agent app context) which pushes each driver with outstanding uncollected CODs a notification listing all their CODs, then the agent composes and sends the app owner a full briefing broken down by driver.",
  "trigger": {
    "condition": null,
    "config": {
      "trigger_type": "scheduled",
      "events": [],
      "schedule_mode": "recurring",
      "cron_expression": "0 9 * * *",
      "one_time_date": null,
      "timezone": "America/Edmonton",
      "interval_value": null,
      "interval_unit": null,
      "interval_anchor": null,
      "ends_type": "never",
      "ends_on_date": null,
      "ends_after_count": null
    }
  },
  "definition": {
    "document": {
      "dsl": "1.0.0",
      "name": "driver_cod_briefing",
      "namespace": "base44",
      "version": "1.0.2"
    },
    "do": [
      {
        "run_and_report": {
          "call": "invoke_superagent_step",
          "then": "end",
          "with": {
            "message": "It is 9am \u2014 the daily driver COD briefing is running now. Follow these steps exactly:\n\n1. Run this bash command (it triggers the RxDeliver briefing function, which sends push notifications to every driver with outstanding uncollected CODs and returns the full grouped JSON):\ncurl -s -X POST 'https://base44.app/api/apps/68570f3cd01bfa2d2408a9d6/functions/driverCodBriefing' -H \"Authorization: Bearer $BASE44_SERVICE_TOKEN\" -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{}'\n\n2. From the returned JSON, compose a compact app-owner briefing in PLAIN TEXT (WhatsApp, no markdown) broken down BY DRIVER. For each driver show a header line like: ROBERT T \u2014 2 CODs, $236.46. Under it, list each item in the format: 09/01 HS \u00b7 $ 36.44 \u00b7 Melinda Martin\nLAYOUT RULE: within each driver block, right-align the money column \u2014 pad all amounts (including the header total) to the same width so every $ sign and decimal lines up vertically.\nEnd with the overall total across drivers. Also note any driver whose push failed (pushes array shows sent/skipped/errors per driver) \u2014 mention delivery failures briefly at the end.\nIf there are no outstanding CODs, just say the COD slate is clean.\n\n3. Broadcast the briefing to the owner via broadcast_message, then stop."
          }
        }
      }
    ]
  }
}